# Trivy image vulnerability suppressions (backend container).
#
# Each entry is an accepted-risk decision, not a scanner error. New
# HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerabilities outside this list still gate the build.
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# ecdsa 0.19.2 — CVE-2024-23342 ("Minerva" timing/side-channel attack).
# No fixed release exists; upstream considers constant-time ECDSA out of
# scope. ecdsa is pulled transitively via python-jose[cryptography]; because
# the [cryptography] extra is installed, JWT ECDSA operations use the
# `cryptography` backend, so the vulnerable code path is not exercised.
CVE-2024-23342

# --- pip's vendored dependencies (pip/_vendor) ---
# The installed top-level msgpack/urllib3/setuptools are already patched in the
# venv. These findings come from the OLD copies pip bundles under
# pip/_vendor (recorded in pip/_vendor/vendor.txt). They are used only
# internally by pip, a build-time tool that is not on the application's runtime
# import or execution path, so they are not exploitable here. Trivy flags them
# regardless of the real top-level versions.
#
# urllib3 (vendored by pip): HTTPS proxy TLS override + chunk-parser DoS.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
CVE-2026-97688
# setuptools (vendored via pip's pkg_resources): path traversal + sdist bypass.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890
# msgpack (vendored by pip): Unpacker reuse out-of-bounds read / DoS.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
